{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <map>\n#include <queue>\n#include <set>\n#include <stack>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long round_to_nearest(long long num, long long den) {\n    long long q = num / den;\n    long long r = num % den;\n    if (r > den - r) q += 1;\n    return q;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    long long best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    for (long long i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long temp = round_to_nearest(x * i, y);\n        long long left = best_den * (x * i - temp * y);\n        long long right = i * (x * best_den - y * best_num);\n        if (abs(left) < abs(right)) {\n            best_num = temp;\n            best_den = i;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef round_to_nearest(num, den):\n    q = num // den\n    r = num